WEBVTT

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:03.960
1. Having tinnitus

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:08.200
2. Feeling down about my life

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.740
3. Drinking too much

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.880
4. Living in a house that is very
old and falling apart

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:21.180
5. People's lack of understanding
about tinnitus Now,

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:26.140
here are some examples
of specific stressful situations.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:31.360
1. Tinnitus that wakes me up

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.880
2. Tinnitus that prevents me from sleeping

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:40.020
3. Drinking too much last weekend

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:46.300
4. The performance evaluation
meeting with my employer tomorrow

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:50.700
5. Bouncing this month's mortgage check

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:54.902
6. Paying income tax
by the yearly deadline Again,

00:00:54.942 --> 00:00:59.995
the reason why we want to think about
the specific type of stress is that usually

00:01:00.035 --> 00:01:05.460
we have more control over specific situations
than generally stressful conditions.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:11.240
You might be thinking right now, how can
I control any issues related to tinnitus?

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:16.460
Please keep going through this course,
and it will become more clear how to do that.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:21.780
To summarize, it is extremely important
to distinguish two types of stress.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.571
Stress that can be changed
and stress that is unchangeable.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:31.700
Remember to use the who, what, when,
where questions that we discussed in slide 7.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:35.124
In a moment, we will highlight
how the type of stress that you

00:01:35.164 --> 00:01:38.680
have identified should match
your choice of coping strategy.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.660
First, we have to describe
coping a little further.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.190
There are two main categories of coping.

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:50.054
A third will be introduced
later in this course.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:53.110
The first is problem solving coping.

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:57.210
This involves reducing, eliminating,
or changing the source of your stress.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:01.990
The second category is what we
call stress relieving strategies.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:04.725
These strategies involve
dealing with your own reactions

00:02:04.765 --> 00:02:07.910
when you cannot change
the source of the stress.

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:12.816
These two types, or categories of coping,
are why it is important to decide

00:02:12.856 --> 00:02:17.130
what is changeable and what
is unchangeable about stressful situations.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:22.327
To explain further, for aspects
of stressful situations that are changeable,

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:25.151
you can use problem solving
strategies to reduce

00:02:25.191 --> 00:02:28.510
or eliminate the specific
source of the stress.

00:02:28.570 --> 00:02:33.830
This focuses on changing something about
the situation that is causing you stress.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:37.990
This will be represented by a green
problems toolbox in the PowerPoint slides.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:42.922
For aspects of stressful situations that
are not changeable, you can use the stress

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:47.750
management strategies to change your reaction
to the specific source of stress.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:50.276
By changing your reactions
to the situation,

00:02:50.316 --> 00:02:55.550
you gain more control and can more
optimally handle what is causing you stress.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:03:01.150
This will be represented by a blue
reactions toolbox in the PowerPoint slides.

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:05.473
One more essential concept
that can help you better use

00:03:05.513 --> 00:03:09.890
the coping strategies that you
have is the concept of fit.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:14.338
The concept of fit means that you
match the type of stress that you

00:03:14.378 --> 00:03:18.690
are experiencing with the type
of coping strategy that you choose.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:21.106
Fitting or matching coping with the type

00:03:21.146 --> 00:03:23.610
of stress is a core
concept for this course.

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:27.459
So make sure that you think about
what it means to fit or match

00:03:27.499 --> 00:03:31.450
the type of stress with the type
of coping that you use.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:34.350
Now to talk more about tinnitus.

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:40.130
As mentioned in previous slides, most
types of tinnitus symptoms are not curable.

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:45.090
Thus, subjective tinnitus is a chronic
impairment at this point in time.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:48.245
Scientific research,
such as on neural regeneration,

00:03:48.285 --> 00:03:51.830
may make tinnitus symptoms
more modifiable in the future.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:56.184
Currently, we tend to think
of tinnitus as unchangeable stress,

00:03:56.224 --> 00:04:01.830
but there is a lot of stress associated
with tinnitus that can be changed.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:06.264
Our working model about coping
with tinnitus is based on a self-management

00:04:06.304 --> 00:04:10.870
perspective, helping you get more
skills to better manage tinnitus.

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:13.158
This involves learning audiological tips

00:04:13.198 --> 00:04:16.070
to manage tinnitus like
we discussed in Section 2.

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:20.211
This also involves learning tips
about coping with stress and thinking

00:04:20.251 --> 00:04:25.050
about what will work best for you
and your own preferences and lifestyle.

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:29.410
You are in the driver's
seat in tinnitus management.

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:33.308
The coping strategies discussed
in the next few sections may help

00:04:33.348 --> 00:04:37.370
your overall stress levels,
not just tinnitus-related stress.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:40.730
It can be helpful for you to reduce
your overall stress levels

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:44.530
because stress may make
your tinnitus symptoms increase.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:48.416
Thinking about how to deal
with your tinnitus,

00:04:48.456 --> 00:04:53.280
the first step is to think about
the specifics of the stress you experience.

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:56.420
What specific aspects can be changed?

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:59.300
What specific aspects cannot be changed?

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:01.740
How do you handle that kind of stress?

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:07.020
After thinking about the type of stress,
then think about the coping you should use.

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:09.100
This is the concept of fit.

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:14.632
As you now know, there are two major groups
of coping strategies to handle stress,

00:05:14.672 --> 00:05:18.980
problem-solving strategies,
and stress-management strategies.

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:24.620
So, think about the issue related
to tinnitus that you want to change or fix.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:29.080
If it is indeed changeable,
then use problem-solving strategies.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:30.269
If it is not changeable,

00:05:30.309 --> 00:05:34.660
then stress-management strategies
are the most appropriate choice.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:39.480
If you try to use problem-solving
strategies with unchangeable stress,

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:42.760
it probably will not
work very well for you.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:47.000
You can exhaust yourself by trying
to change what is unchangeable.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:49.845
You may be frustrated
or angry about not being able

00:05:49.885 --> 00:05:53.920
to change something that is, in reality,
not changeable.

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:58.200
So the most effective way of handling
stressful situations is to match,

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:02.440
or fit, the type of coping strategy
to the type of stressful situation.

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:07.250
This coping with tinnitus course will
give you more ideas for these two coping

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:11.915
approaches, plus a third category,
which we will discuss in an upcoming section,

00:06:11.955 --> 00:06:16.740
to help you have more control over
the impact of tinnitus on your life.

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:22.840
Let us practice the concept
of fit to tinnitus for a moment.

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.946
Think about what
is changeable and unchangeable

00:06:25.986 --> 00:06:28.280
about these two stressful situations.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.340
Example 1.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:34.380
You need to tell a new friend
that you have tinnitus.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.600
Consider what is changeable.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:41.160
You have control over how and when
to tell your friend about tinnitus.

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:43.880
Consider what is unchangeable.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:47.560
You do not have control
over how your friend reacts.

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:50.760
But most likely,
they will react with sympathy.

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:54.780
If they do not react the way you
want them to, then you can use some

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:59.520
of the stress management strategies
that we teach in upcoming sections.

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:02.080
Example 2.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:06.988
You are worrying about how to sleep
at night when your tinnitus is flaring up.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:09.080
Consider what is changeable.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:12.197
Using some of the audiological
strategies we taught

00:07:12.237 --> 00:07:15.580
in section 2 may help
you in this circumstance.

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:20.490
Otherwise, you may develop insomnia
due to fear of not getting to sleep

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:24.820
and worrying about being too tired
during the next day to function well.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:27.640
Consider what is unchangeable.

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:31.020
The fact that you will
have tinnitus tonight.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:35.780
Many of the stress management techniques
taught in this course can be useful

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:41.520
to help relax you, especially when used
in addition to the audiological strategies.
